winewayland: enable the owned-subsurface gates by default

NEUTRON_OWNED_SUBSURFACE_CAPTIONED and NEUTRON_OWNED_ZORDER now default ON; =0 disables.

Both were off for real reasons, and both reasons are now fixed:

  * CAPTIONED was turned off after 11.10-64, where promoting captioned owned windows sank
    every plugin panel behind the Program Monitor and froze Premiere on a file dialog. The
    sinking was the place_above(parent) demote fixed in zzzzzzzzzzzc -- place_above(parent)
    means directly above the PARENT'S OWN CONTENT, i.e. the bottom of the sibling stack.
    The file dialog is the modal case, excluded by neutron_owned_subsurface_modal().

  * OWNED_ZORDER was off because place_above against a non-sibling is a FATAL protocol error
    (kwin: "error in client communication", process dies with no Wine backtrace, measured
    2026-08-27 and only with this gate on). Guarded twice now: the sibling-validity check in
    restack_apply's owned branch, and the union role guard from zzzzzzzzzzzc.

Evidence for flipping them, not just for the fixes:

  * Build tester, 11.10-72, ordinary untraced session with these switches on: SIX consecutive
    plugin-panel docks, no freeze; a File dialog opened and dismissed -- the other half of the
    64 regression -- on the same switch set.
  * Dev box, operator-confirmed: drag-to-dock lands on target ("drag lands on target now"),
    and the panel no longer sinks behind the Program Monitor ("no sink").

Without CAPTIONED an owned panel stays an independent xdg_toplevel, whose position is the
compositor's and never ours, so a dock drag is off by the divergence between where Wine thinks
the window is and where it actually is. Without OWNED_ZORDER promoted owned windows are never
ordered at all and keep whatever stacking they were inserted with.

⚠️ Known-not-established: six docks is a rate, not proof of absence; nothing was done to provoke
the original deadlock race; no pre-fix contrast build was run. The operator also reports the panel
still sinks behind the drop HIGHLIGHT specifically, which predates this change and is untouched.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -2333,7 +2333,15 @@
 static BOOL neutron_owned_zorder(void)
 {
     static int on = -1;
-    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_OWNED_ZORDER"); on = (e && e[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0; }
+    /* NEUTRON: DEFAULT ON since 2026-09-01 (11.10-73). Was OFF because place_above against a
+     * non-sibling is a FATAL protocol error -- kwin answers "error in client communication" and
+     * Premiere dies with no Wine backtrace (measured 2026-08-27, only with this on). Fixed twice
+     * over: the sibling-validity check in restack_apply's owned branch, and the union role guard
+     * (wl_subsurface/toplevel_hwnd alias xdg_toplevel/xdg_toplevel_icon when the role is not
+     * SUBSURFACE, so every toplevel looked like a subsurface and was excluded only by luck).
+     * Without this, promoted owned windows are never ordered at all. Kill switch:
+     * NEUTRON_OWNED_ZORDER=0. */
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_OWNED_ZORDER"); on = (e && e[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1; }
     return on;
 }
 
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -385,7 +385,17 @@
      * window and freezing on a file dialog is not a trade we get to make on someone's working
      * machine. Set to 1 to opt in. */
     static int on = -1;
-    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_OWNED_SUBSURFACE_CAPTIONED"); on = (e && e[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0; }
+    /* NEUTRON: DEFAULT ON since 2026-09-01 (11.10-73). Turned OFF after 11.10-64, where promoting
+     * captioned owned windows sank every plugin panel behind the Program Monitor and froze Premiere
+     * on a file dialog. Both blockers are fixed and operator-confirmed: the sinking was the
+     * place_above(parent) demote (neutron_no_demote), and the modal case is excluded by
+     * neutron_owned_subsurface_modal(). Build tester 2026-09-01 on 11.10-72 with these on: six
+     * consecutive plugin-panel docks, a File dialog opened and dismissed, no freeze. Dev box:
+     * drag-to-dock lands on target, no sink.
+     * What it buys: an owned window gets a coordinate space its owner can actually hit, which is
+     * what a dock drag needs -- an xdg_toplevel's position is the compositor's, never ours.
+     * Kill switch: NEUTRON_OWNED_SUBSURFACE_CAPTIONED=0. */
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_OWNED_SUBSURFACE_CAPTIONED"); on = (e && e[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1; }
     return on;
 }
 
